Filed by cardmem (#1022) on Christian's order: classify('ucat_01M3…') → null
on 0.9.3, so the vault could not autodetect an UpCloud token and nothing in
the fleet redacted one.

  ucat_ + exactly 26 Crockford base32 (a ULID)     label upcloud-api-token

The shape is measured at the source, not derived from the masked example:
UpCloud's API docs (ucat_01DQE3AJDEBFEKECFM558TGH2F), UpCloud's own Go
client fixture (ucat_01DEADBEEFDEADBEEFDEADBEEF), and Kingfisher's rule.
Case-insensitive; trailing lookahead so 27 chars does not match its first
26, and UpCloud's own ucat_[REDACTED] marker stays readable.

Mutation-checked: breaking the label reddens 3 of the 9 new tests; dropping
the length to {25} without the lookahead reddens 2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
